.SH NAME
install.sh \- modular installer for Prometheus Dotfiles

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B install.sh
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
[\fB\-\-yes\fR]
[\fB\-\-only=\fIMODULES\fR]
[\fB\-\-skip=\fIMODULES\fR]
[\fB\-\-modules\fR]
[\fB\-\-man\fR]
[\fB\-\-help\fR]
.PP
.B INSTALL_MODULES=\fIMODULES\fR install.sh

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B install.sh
is a modular dotfiles installer for macOS. Each major step (Homebrew,
window manager, symlinks, LaunchAgents, macOS tweaks, etc.) lives in its
own file under
.IR install.d/ .
The orchestrator parses flags, presents an interactive arrow-key picker
to select which modules to run, then sources and calls each selected
module's
.B module_<name>()
function in dependency order.
.PP
The interactive picker is pure bash \(em no
.B whiptail
or
.B dialog
dependency \(em so it works on a fresh macOS install where nothing extra
has been brewed yet. Arrow keys move the cursor, Space toggles the
highlighted module, Enter confirms and runs.
.PP
The script is idempotent: re-running it after a successful install
detects what's already in place and skips it.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Preview every action the script would take without making any changes.
Symlinks are not created, Homebrew is not invoked, no
.B defaults write
runs. Useful for auditing a fresh install or seeing what's left to do
on a configured machine. Combines with any other flag.
.TP
.BR \-\-yes ", " \-y
Run all modules with auto-Yes for every sub-prompt. Skips the interactive
picker entirely. Equivalent to selecting everything in the picker.
.TP
\fB\-\-only=\fIMODULES\fR
Comma-separated list of modules to run (skips the picker). Mutually
exclusive with
.BR \-\-skip .
Example:
.BR "\-\-only=symlinks,macos" .
.TP
\fB\-\-skip=\fIMODULES\fR
Comma-separated list of modules to skip. All others run. Mutually
exclusive with
.BR \-\-only .
.TP
.B \-\-modules
Print the available module list and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-man
Open this man page in your pager.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Print a short usage summary and exit.

.SH MODULES
The following modules are available. Order below is the run order, not
the menu order. Modules can be combined freely.
.TP
.B symlinks
Dotfile symlinks
.RB ( ~/.zshrc ", " ~/.zprofile ", " ~/.config/* ", " ~/.local/bin/* ,
fish functions, AeroSpace config when applicable). Pre-checked in the
picker by default \(em this is the core of dotfiles management.
.TP
.B homebrew
Homebrew install + Brewfile bundle (core CLI tools, fonts), Node.js LTS
via nvm, Bun via its own installer, WM-specific Brewfile when a WM is
chosen, SketchyBar app font.
.TP
.B wm
Window manager picker \(em OmniWM, AeroSpace, or none. Sets
.B WM_CHOICE
which gates downstream WM-specific behavior in the other modules.
.TP
.B apps
Optional GUI apps (per-app Y/N prompts): Ghostty terminal, Cursor editor,
Claude Code CLI, Claude Desktop, OpenAI Codex CLI, Spotify, plus a
Starship statusline configurer for Claude Code.
.TP
.B macos
macOS preferences via
.BR defaults (1):
Dock auto-hide delay, Finder tweaks, tap-to-click, screenshot location,
Mission Control space order, Microsoft Office telemetry off, battery
percentage, and other quality-of-life adjustments.
.TP
.B launchd
Background agents \(em monthly Time Machine LaunchDaemon (replaces
Apple's hourly schedule) and the sort-downloads LaunchAgent (auto-sorts
.B ~/Downloads
and
.B ~/Pictures/Screenshots
to the TrueNAS share at
.BR /Volumes/media/ ).
.TP
.B shells
Shell plugins that don't ship via Homebrew \(em currently
.B fzf-tab
(git-cloned to
.IR ~/.local/share/zsh/ ).
.TP
.B sketchybar
Restart the SketchyBar service to pick up new config. Auto-skips when
no WM is selected.

.SH INTERACTIVE PICKER
When no selection flag is given, the script opens a numbered picker:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
[x] symlinks    \- Dotfile symlinks
[ ] homebrew    \- Homebrew + Brewfile + Node + Bun
[ ] wm          \- Window manager (OmniWM / AeroSpace / none)
[ ] apps        \- Optional GUI apps
[ ] macos       \- macOS preferences
[ ] launchd     \- LaunchAgents
[ ] shells      \- Shell plugins (fzf-tab)
[ ] sketchybar  \- SketchyBar restart
.EE
.RE
.PP
Keys:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
\fB\(ua\fR / \fBk\fR     Move cursor up
\fB\(da\fR / \fBj\fR     Move cursor down
\fBSpace\fR     Toggle the highlighted module
\fBa\fR         Select all
\fBn\fR         Clear all
\fBr\fR         Reset to defaults (symlinks only)
\fBEnter\fR     Confirm and run
\fBq\fR / \fBEsc\fR   Quit (clears selection, bails out)
.fi
.RE

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Default \(em open the interactive picker:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
\fB./install.sh\fR
.EE
.RE
.PP
Preview every action without making changes:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
\fB./install.sh \-\-dry\-run\fR
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run only the symlink and macOS modules:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
\fB./install.sh \-\-only=symlinks,macos\fR
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run everything except the window manager and Homebrew install:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
\fB./install.sh \-\-skip=wm,homebrew\fR
.EE
.RE
.PP
CI-friendly run \(em all modules, auto-Yes to every prompt:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
\fB./install.sh \-\-yes\fR
.EE
.RE
.PP
Equivalent of
.B \-\-only
via environment variable (useful when piping the script through
.BR bash (1)):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
\fBINSTALL_MODULES=symlinks,macos ./install.sh\fR
.EE
.RE
.PP
Remote one-liner \(em clones the repo, then runs the installer:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
\fBcurl \-fsSL https://dotfiles.rafay99.com/install.sh | bash\fR
.EE
.RE

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B INSTALL_MODULES
Comma-separated list of modules to run, equivalent to
.BR \-\-only .
Honored only when no selection flag is given on the command line.
Useful for scripted invocations and the curl bootstrap.

.SH FILES
.TP
.B install.sh
The orchestrator. Parses flags, presents the picker, runs modules.
.TP
.B install.d/
Module directory.
.TP
.B install.d/00-lib.sh
Shared helpers: colors, logging,
.BR prompt ,
.BR link ,
.BR brew_install ,
.BR npm_install ,
.BR curl_install ,
.BR configure_claude_statusline .
.TP
.B install.d/01-menu.sh
Module catalog, selection state, interactive picker, flag parsing.
.TP
.BR install.d/10-prereqs.sh "  through  " install.d/90-sketchybar.sh
The actual module implementations. Each defines exactly one function:
.BR module_<name>() .
.TP
.B Brewfile
Core Homebrew formula list. Always applied when the
.B homebrew
module runs.
.TP
.B Brewfile.omniwm
Additional formulae for OmniWM (only applied when WM = omniwm).
.TP
.B Brewfile.aerospace
Additional formulae for AeroSpace (only applied when WM = aerospace).
.TP
.B install.sh.backup
A frozen pre-modularization copy of
.BR install.sh ,
kept temporarily as a safety net. Delete once the modular installer
has been validated.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success \(em all selected modules completed without errors.
.TP
.B 1
One or more errors were recorded. See the summary at the end of the run
for the
.B Errors
section listing what failed.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by the user (Ctrl-C or Esc from the picker).

